        "description": "<div id=\"remove_no_follow\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid grid--cols-10@md grid--cols-8@lg article-column \">\n\t\t\t\t\t  <div class=\"col-12 col-10@md col-6@lg col-start-3@lg\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"article-column__content\">\n<section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For the past few years, most enterprise AI has been advisory. It summarized tickets, drafted knowledge articles, and suggested next steps. A person still decided what to do.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That\u2019s changing. Agentic AI systems can plan multistep tasks and carry them out: querying systems, triggering workflows, changing configurations, and closing tickets with little or no human involvement. <a href=\"https://www.ivanti.com/resources/research-reports/state-of-cybersecurity-report?utm_source=foundry&amp;utm_medium=hosted-content&amp;utm_campaign=2026-global-Q3Q4TL-foundry-brandpost-computer-world&amp;utm_content=state-of-cybersecurity-report&amp;elqCa",
